WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.490
As an actor, having someone who looks exactly
like you can give you a big advantage.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:10.030
While some duos, like the Olsen twins or Dylan
and Cole Sprouse, have made it a part of their

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.460
brand, here are some stars that you may not
have realized have an identical twin.

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.100
In 2009, Jill Hennessy spoke with Contact
Music about the burdens her identical twin

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.210
Jacqueline often faces, saying,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:25.440
"She gets stalked by people who don't believe
she's my twin.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.619
She'll very kindly say, 'I'm Jack, her sister,'
and they'll think she's lying.

00:00:29.619 --> 00:00:32.619
They think it's really Jill Hennessy just
being really bitchy!"

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:36.690
While Jacqueline and her sister Jill have
each carved out separate accomplished careers

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:41.680
on their own — the former has a Ph.D. in
French literature, is a journalist and TV

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.760
host, and the latter was Claire Kincaid on
"Law &amp; Order" and the titular character on

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.140
"Crossing Jordan" — the sisters have collaborated
several times in film and music.

00:00:50.140 --> 00:00:54.600
They once had a duo called Jack and Jill,
were buskers in Toronto's subways, and still

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.489
sing together to this day.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:02.399
The pair made their film debut together, playing
twin escorts in David Cronenberg's 1988 drama

00:01:02.399 --> 00:01:03.399
"Dead Ringers."

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:07.749
In the 1996 "Law &amp; Order" episode "Corpus
Delicti", Jacqueline literally stood in for

00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:11.899
her sister for courtroom scenes while Jill
was off shooting a crossover episode with

00:01:11.899 --> 00:01:14.100
"Homicide: Life on the Street."

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.200
When Jill wrote and directed 2000's "The Acting
Class," she was sure to include her older

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:19.590
sister in the roll call.

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:25.319
While Rami Malek hit the big time as Elliot
on TV's "Mr. Robot," and as Freddie Mercury

00:01:25.319 --> 00:01:30.710
in the biopic "Bohemian Rhapsody," his identical
twin brother Sami has been spending his time

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.740
handing out grades as a teacher in Los Angeles.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:37.530
Sami currently teaches English as a Second
Language at a middle school.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:42.200
The only time Sami gets into character and
costume is to protest and demand changes for

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:43.200
schools.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.359
He's very passionate about his vocation, and
is known to fight for both teachers and students

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:48.359
alike.

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:52.649
The closest Sami gets to the limelight is
to celebrate his brother's success, particularly

00:01:52.649 --> 00:01:57.639
at the 2019 Academy Awards when Rami took
home the Best Actor award, saying in a red

00:01:57.639 --> 00:01:58.639
carpet interview,

00:01:58.639 --> 00:02:00.419
"My boy had it in the bag.

00:02:00.419 --> 00:02:01.600
He killed it."

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.329
Rami has also joked that his success in film
and TV is likely to give his brother a boost

00:02:06.329 --> 00:02:07.969
in his romantic life.

00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:09.590
During an appearance on "Jimmy Kimmel Live!"

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:13.989
Rami told a switcheroo story where he came
to Sami's aid when he needed to do a Greek

00:02:13.989 --> 00:02:17.379
monologue for a class in order to graduate
from UCLA.

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:20.849
When Sami's teacher was floored by the performance,
Rami responded,

00:02:20.849 --> 00:02:23.379
"Oh… it's just a hobby."

00:02:25.549 --> 00:02:29.910
The first transgender person to be nominated
for an Emmy, Laverne Cox got her breakout

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:34.629
role as Sophia Burset, a charismatic inmate
in "Orange is the New Black."

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:39.250
When it came time to film flashback scenes
featuring Sophia before her transition, however,

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:43.390
it was easy to find the perfect fit: Laverne's
twin brother.

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:48.500
Going by the name M Lamar, the avant-garde
artist is an operatic countertenor and pianist

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:53.470
whose music is frequently blended with film,
sculpture, installation and performance.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.860
The twins had a difficult time growing up
and being different in their hometown of Mobile,

00:02:57.860 --> 00:02:58.860
Alabama.

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.329
They were constantly bullied at school, but
their mother Gloria impressed upon them the

00:03:02.329 --> 00:03:07.109
importance of education, telling the local
paper in 2019 that she, quote, "groomed them

00:03:07.109 --> 00:03:08.670
for success."

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:13.420
While Laverne is out and proud, Lamar takes
a more subdued approach, as he told World

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.840
of Wonder in 2016.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:18.790
"What I do is not designed to cross over to
the mainstream.

00:03:18.790 --> 00:03:19.920
That's not my goal.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.370
I'm not looking for that sort of fame or recognition."

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:27.739
However, Lamar did indeed step into the mainstream
on one occasion, when he played the pre-transition

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:32.579
version of Sophia Burset in the season one
"Orange is the New Black" episode "Lesbian

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.829
Request Denied."

00:03:33.829 --> 00:03:38.799
Cox originally wanted to play the role herself,
but she told the Huffington Post in 2013 that

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:42.739
the episode's director, Jodie Foster, quote,
"didn't think [she] looked masculine enough

00:03:42.739 --> 00:03:43.739
to play a guy."

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.629
Harriet Norton told the Louisville Courier-Journal
in 1971 about her famous sister:

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:54.689
"We used to say we'd both be in the theater,
me on Broadway and her in the operating theater.

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:56.930
But she's the one who got into show business."

00:03:56.930 --> 00:04:01.439
Norton's twin sister was none other than Ann
B. Davis, known for playing the lovable and

00:04:01.439 --> 00:04:04.420
ever-dependable housekeeper Alice on "The
Brady Bunch."

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:09.040
Ann found early success on "The Bob Cummings
Show" in the role of Schultzy, which won her

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:13.310
back-to-back Emmy awards in 1958 and 1959.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:16.150
After the second win, Harriet wired her sister
the message,

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.650
"One of us was bound to have twins."

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.860
Harriet was given the chance to join Ann in
a Schultzy "double" episode, but couldn't

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:25.270
handle the lines, so the idea was scrapped.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.080
That probably explains why Harriet wasn't
enlisted to play Alice's identical cousin

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.330
"Sergeant Emma" on the "Brady Bunch" episode
of the same name, where Ann ended up taking

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.169
on both roles herself.

00:04:36.169 --> 00:04:40.380
Regardless, the two maintained an unwavering
bond throughout their entire lives.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.669
Ann died in 2014, at age 88.

00:04:43.669 --> 00:04:47.900
She never married and is survived by Harriet,
who currently resides in Tucson, Arizona.

00:04:49.229 --> 00:04:54.050
Bonar Bain never missed a chance to take a
playful swipe at his more famous brother,

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:58.300
Conrad Bain of TV's "Maude" and "Diff'rent
Strokes," telling the Ottawa Citizen,

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.750
"He's 20 minutes older than I am and he looks
every minute of it."

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.590
The two Bain boys were dedicated to their
local dramatic arts program in their teen

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.419
years, trading off lead roles in their school
plays.

00:05:08.419 --> 00:05:12.919
When Conrad headed to New York to advance
his acting career, Bonar chose a different,

00:05:12.919 --> 00:05:17.940
more stable path back in Edmonton, developing
a successful career in the airline, rental

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.440
car and parking businesses.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:23.200
However, that didn't stop him from taking
an occasional part.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:27.250
When the writers of "Maude" drummed up an
episode involving the escaped-convict twin

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.139
of Conrad's character Arthur, Conrad lamented,

00:05:30.139 --> 00:05:31.669
"I knew we were in trouble.

00:05:31.669 --> 00:05:34.660
The scriptwriters had my brother as a sex
maniac."

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:39.199
In the end, Conrad played both parts and Bonar,
quote, "only came in for two lines at the

00:05:39.199 --> 00:05:43.000
end when he [got] caught, but everybody thought
it was him the whole time."

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:47.500
A similar experience took place on the "The
Van Drummonds" episode of "Strokes."

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:51.699
Conrad played their Dutch cousin Anna Van
Drummond, and in the scenes where Philip appeared

00:05:51.699 --> 00:05:54.139
alongside her, Bonar acted as a stand-in.

00:05:54.139 --> 00:06:00.330
Bonar went solo a few other times, most memorably
spoofing Conrad as alien double agent "Hank

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:04.199
Bain" on "SCTV," appearing in a sketch called
"Different Folks."

00:06:04.199 --> 00:06:09.380
Back in the 1940s, Conrad was set to be an
extra in a Canadian war propaganda film, but

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:10.949
got sick right before the shoot.

00:06:10.949 --> 00:06:13.040
Bonar stepped in for his brother, and remembered:

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:17.050
"The casting director took one look at me
and said, 'What difference does it make?'"

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.229
Bonar passed away in 2005, at age 82.

00:06:20.229 --> 00:06:22.550
Conrad followed in 2013, at age 89.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:27.690
Before Linda Hamilton was trying to escape
from "The Terminator," she was performing

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:32.759
in community children's theater back in Salisbury,
Maryland alongside her sister Leslie, who

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:34.889
was born six minutes after she was.

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.220
Linda recalled in 1987:

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:40.020
"We would be cast in the same role and work
alternate performances.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:41.289
It was a real gimmick."

00:06:41.289 --> 00:06:45.560
While Linda made the jump to Hollywood, Leslie
followed her own passion by becoming a nurse

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:46.960
and caretaker.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.120
Leslie does have one credit to her name, however,
and it's in one of the greatest action films

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.120
of all time: she played a cyborg imitation
of Sarah Connor in "Terminator 2: Judgment

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:59.490
Day," and was paid a thousand dollars for
her time and effort.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.860
Being on set not only gave Leslie a glimpse
of the Hollywood limelight, but also a taste

00:07:03.860 --> 00:07:09.710
of the fun too, as she once even Arnold Schwarzenegger
himself into thinking she was Linda.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:12.600
One film was more than enough for Leslie,
however.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:16.860
After vowing to never return to the franchise,
Linda changed her tune and suited back up

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:20.289
as Sarah Connor in 2019's "Terminator: Dark
Fate."

00:07:20.289 --> 00:07:22.780
Leslie passed away in 2020 at age 63.

00:07:24.599 --> 00:07:29.199
When the writers for "Days of Our Lives" asked
their star Deidre Hall if there were any storylines

00:07:29.199 --> 00:07:33.539
she'd like to pursue, she was quick to pitch
the idea of giving her character, Dr. Marlena

00:07:33.539 --> 00:07:35.120
Evans, a twin sister.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.040
Not long after, Deirdre's sister Andrea took
a break from her summer job as a special education

00:07:40.040 --> 00:07:42.389
teacher to play Marlena's jealous twin Samantha.

00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:46.660
The job spilled beyond the summer, and ended
up lasting several seasons.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:51.300
The first time the pair acted together was
in 1977, in the Krofft brothers cult classic

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.379
show "Electra Woman and Dyna Girl," where
Andrea played Deirdre's clone.

00:07:56.379 --> 00:08:00.819
Andrea returned to "Days of Our Lives" in
2000 when she showed up as Hattie Adams, a

00:08:00.819 --> 00:08:03.830
woman who just so happens to look exactly
like Marlena.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.240
The pandemic turned into a mixed blessing
for the twins, who got to spend over nine

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.090
weeks together for the first time since their
youth.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.090
Andrea gushed,

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:13.860
"It's like find­ing your best friend again.

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:14.860
It's been grand.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.580
[…] [P]aint­ing is so much fun, but we
just mostly laughed."

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:23.789
In 2007, Jon Heder told Elle magazine that
his relationship with twin Daniel is like

00:08:23.789 --> 00:08:24.789
a marriage.

00:08:24.789 --> 00:08:28.930
"My brother and I think alike, know everything
about one another, and when we get together,

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.610
we block everything else out.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.700
Nothing exists in our world except for us."

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:39.270
The Heder boys were always artistic, and followed
their brother Doug to BYU to study animation.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:44.050
Jon found everlasting fame playing the title
role in 2004's "Napoleon Dynamite," then went

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:47.470
on to star in such films as "Blades of Glory"
and "The Benchwarmers."

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:52.240
Daniel is a visual effects artist who has
worked on blockbuster films like "Alita: Battle

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.170
Angel" and "Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:59.430
He also worked as an animator on 2006's "Monster
House," where his brother Jon provided a voice

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:00.430
over.

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:04.050
The two have acted together in a few short
films, and Ashton Kutcher helped Daniel prank

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:07.130
Jon in a 2005 episode of "Punk'd."

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:11.010
Along with their older brother Doug, they
formed Greasy Entertainment and have several

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:14.600
projects in the works — including, of course,
some animated ones.

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.650
As for being twins outside of work?

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:20.470
Jon has admitted that they switched classrooms
for a day in sixth grade — but the scheme

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:24.620
backfired when Daniel took a pop quiz he obviously
wasn't prepared for.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:30.300
Jon Heder wasn't the only twin to star in
"Napoleon Dynamite," as Efren Ramirez got

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.830
a vote of confidence as the titular hero's
best friend Pedro.

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:38.420
Efren and his identical twin Carlos were discovered
on the street by Robert Blake, who got them

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:40.420
roles in his series "Hell Town."

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:44.551
Carlos took a break from acting in 1991 and
joined the United States Air Force, but when

00:09:44.551 --> 00:09:48.270
Efren's career skyrocketed, he returned to
the craft.

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:52.370
The two appeared together in "Potheads: The
Movie," as well as the high-octane action

00:09:52.370 --> 00:09:55.520
movie "Crank" and its sequel, "Crank: High
Voltage."

00:09:55.520 --> 00:10:00.450
They shared screen time and many good times
in real life, throwing famously raucous dual

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.020
birthday bashes.

00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:06.530
Unfortunately, the story of the Ramirez brothers
doesn't have the happiest of endings.

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:11.490
The Ramirez twins had a falling out over Carlos
making public appearances as Efren... without

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.200
his brother's consent.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:18.780
According to a 2013 TMZ report, Efren threatened
to sue his brother for 10 million dollars

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:21.750
in 2008, and they hadn't spoken since.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:23.580
Carlos told TMZ at the time,

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:27.580
"I think it's safe to say the magnitude of
'Napoleon Dynamite' and everything that has

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:31.040
come along with it has ruined my relationship
with my twin."

00:10:31.040 --> 00:10:35.560
As of present day, both Ramirez brothers are
still making appearances in films and TV series

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:36.790
— just not together.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:41.570
If you've ever wondered what it's like to
have a celebrity doppelganger who's starring

00:10:41.570 --> 00:10:47.180
in one of the most successful shows of the
1990s, firefighter Caroline Paul detailed

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:53.750
exactly how it feels in her 2015 book "Almost
Her: The Strange Dilemma of Being Nearly Famous."

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:57.710
"The possibility of an identical twin never
crossed anyone's mind.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:02.210
It was easier to believe that the 'Baywatch'
star had decided to swaddle herself in a turnout

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:06.850
coat and helmet, grab that ax, and jump on
a fire engine for the day."

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:11.670
Caroline's slightly older twin sister is actress
Alexandra Paul, who made a splash on TV as

00:11:11.670 --> 00:11:14.640
Stephanie Holden for 5 seasons of "Baywatch."

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:18.661
She's also made appearances in films like
"Christine," "8 Million Ways to Die," and

00:11:18.661 --> 00:11:20.140
"Dragnet."

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:24.360
Caroline never joined the acting business
herself, but did work on "Christine" as Alexandra's

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:28.260
stand-in on set, confusing director John Carpenter
in the process.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:33.550
Alexandra told the Ohio News-Journal in 1999
how deep her bond runs with Caroline:

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:36.450
"I'll always have her, even if everything
else goes badly.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.560
It's like having your left arm or something.

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:39.830
She means everything to me."

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:44.870
Despite what you might think on first look,
Sidra Smith has something to say:

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:49.250
"I am not the lady from the Tyler Perry movie!"

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:53.860
It's an easy mistake to make — her identical
twin sister Tasha is indeed the lady from

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:59.740
the Tyler Perry movie, having starred in 2007's
"Why Did I Get Married?" and its 2010 sequel.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.480
In a 2017 Instagram post, Sidra teased,

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:03.910
"I'm the oldest twin.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:08.210
I always say that I came out first because
she KICKED me OUT so she could be in our mothers

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:10.420
belly ALONE for 2 minutes."

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:14.870
The sisters overcame a tough upbringing and
both left their hometown of Camden, New Jersey

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:16.580
for greener pastures.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:20.660
While Tasha made appearances in films like
"Couples Retreat" and shows like "Empire,"

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:22.650
Sidra became a casting director.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:26.650
Despite their difference in occupation, the
two always strive to help each other in their

00:12:26.650 --> 00:12:29.560
endeavors, with Tasha telling NPR in 2008,

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.290
"My sister is my business partner, my twin.

00:12:32.290 --> 00:12:34.310
She's an amazing producer, writer.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:38.350
You know, we're just grinding and trying to
make my mother proud as well as God."

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:42.600
The two did appear on screen together once,
getting the opportunity to say a single word

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:45.240
between the two of them in the film "Twin
Sitters."

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:50.320
While they have confused many fans in public,
they also have fooled the technology of Apple,

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:54.860
proving that identical twins can pass for
the other when using iPhone's face activation

00:12:54.860 --> 00:12:56.870
security feature.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:00.990
Nicholas Brendon had dreams of playing for
the Dodgers, but an injury took him off the

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.910
baseball diamond and onto a TV set.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:08.881
Nicholas found early success as Xander Harris
in "Buffy the Vampire Slayer," while his brother

00:13:08.881 --> 00:13:12.880
Kelly took industry jobs behind the scenes
as a set decorator.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:17.350
When Kelly finally decided to join his brother
in the limelight, he landed a role on "Buffy"

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:21.080
as a Xander double in the season five episode
"The Replacement".

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:26.170
The pair also appeared together for several
episodes of "Hollywood Squares" and the mind-bending

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:29.020
2013 horror film "Coherence."

00:13:29.020 --> 00:13:32.890
Despite Kelly's later start, Nicholas has
always been happy to boost his brother in

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:34.320
any way he can.

00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:39.220
In 1999, Nicholas told Teen People that the
duo have a very special relationship, saying,

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:43.880
"There's this unexplained twin phenomenon
that even we can't understand."

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:48.640
The two have so much in common, in fact, that
they've been known to spontaneously belt out

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:53.080
the same song at the exact same time, and
have even had similar recurring dreams.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:59.610
Actress Lorraine Vélez is very close with
her slightly younger sister, but not too close:

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.300
she once told Latin Heat,

00:14:01.300 --> 00:14:03.790
"My sister is part of my journey, but not
all of it.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:05.620
I exist as an individual."

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:10.260
Lorraine's twin sister, Luna Lauren Vélez,
is also an actress, singer, and dancer.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:15.380
The Vélez twins both attended the Alvin Ailey
Dance school, then studied acting at The Acting

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:16.380
Studio.

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:20.500
Lorraine headed to the West End of London
where she starred in musicals like "Miss Saigon,"

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:25.680
"Fame," and "Rent," but she later returned
to the States to pursue further creative endeavours.

00:14:25.680 --> 00:14:30.991
At the same time, Luna was becoming a recognizable
face to audiences on TV shows such as "New

00:14:30.991 --> 00:14:34.310
York Undercover," "Oz," "Ugly Betty," and
"Dexter."

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:39.270
The two have a single shared credit to their
names — the 2002 "Hitman" episode of "Law

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.480
&amp; Order" — but never actually share the
screen during its runtime.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.860
That doesn't mean the two don't spend time
together when they're off camera, however

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:49.920
— Luna consistently shares photos of the
pair together on her Instagram, especially

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.444
on #TwinTuesday.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:57.620
Being identical was particularly rough going
on the Laurance brothers, who both decided

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:00.110
to become actors at the same time.

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:01.440
Matthew said to Entertainment Weekly,

00:15:01.440 --> 00:15:05.930
"If you have to pick a business not to go
into with an identical twin, this is it.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:07.650
We didn't talk for a long time."

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:13.731
Best known for cleaning teeth as David Silver's
dad Mel on "Beverly Hills, 90210," Matthew

00:15:13.731 --> 00:15:16.280
was born four minutes later than his twin.

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:20.670
Elder brother Mitchell shared his twin’s
opinions on the entertainment business, saying,

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:23.070
"At times I hate the fact that Matthew's here.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:26.420
We have moments of closeness and a lot of
times of conflict."

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:30.740
The two were able to get past their differences
and collaborated several times, including

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:34.700
for a pair of "Cop Rock" episodes and an appearance
on "The Commish."

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:39.800
On "Saturday Night Live," Matthew was a featured
player in Season 6, while Mitchell held various

00:15:39.800 --> 00:15:42.390
roles, eventually becoming an associate director.

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:46.580
In the memorable "Outer Limits" episode "In
Another Life," Mitchell played a man trapped

00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:50.740
in an alternate reality, surrounded by many
different versions of himself, which were

00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:52.870
played by both he and Matthew.

00:15:52.870 --> 00:15:57.010
When Mitchell decided it was time to leave
the soap opera "Santa Barbara" and move on

00:15:57.010 --> 00:16:00.600
to "Reasonable Doubts," Matthew was there
to take his place.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:05.191
The two have since moved away from Hollywood
and into the world of golf podcasting: Matthew

00:16:05.191 --> 00:16:10.950
hosts the "Backspin Golf" radio show and podcast
for ESPN, while Mitchell is the Co-Host and

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:14.980
Co-Producer of "Talking GolfGetaways with
Mitch &amp; Darin."

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.270
